        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.064,
            0.378,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.121,
            0.885,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "As we saw in the discussion above, if 75 was a multiple of 21, then all prime factors of 21 would also be prime factors of 75. However, 7 is a prime factor of 21 but not a prime factor of 75. Therefore, 75 is not divisible by 21."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.219,
            0.873,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": "**Example:** Is 42 divisible by 12? Find the prime factorisations of both:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.36,
            0.245,
            0.689,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": "42=2\\times3\\times7\\  and \\ 12=2\\times2\\times3",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.272,
            0.885,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": "All prime factors of 12 are also prime factors of 42. But the prime factorisation of 12 is not included in the prime factorisation of 42. This is because 2 occurs twice in the prime factorisation of 12 but only once in the prime factorisation of 42. This means that 42 is not divisible by 12."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.386,
            0.885,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": "We can say that if one number is divisible by another, then the prime factorisation of the second number is included in the prime factorisation of the first number."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.466,
            0.353,
            0.488
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.495,
            0.884,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "1. Are the following pairs of numbers co-prime? Guess first and then use prime factorisation to verify your answer. a. 30 and 45 b. 57 and 85 c. 121 and 1331 d. 343 and 216"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.586,
            0.883,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "2. Is the first number divisible by the second? Use prime factorisation. a. 225 and 27 b. 96 and 24 c. 343 and 17 d. 999 and 99"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.655,
            0.885,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": "3. The first number has prime factorisation 2 × 3 × 7 and the second number has prime factorisation 3 × 7 × 11. Are they co-prime? Does one of them divide the other?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.723,
            0.878,
            0.743
          ],
          "content": "4. Guna says, “Any two prime numbers are co-prime?”. Is he right?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.771,
            0.466,
            0.797
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "5.5 Divisibility Tests"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.811,
            0.885,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": "So far, we have been finding factors of numbers in different contexts, including to determine if a number is prime or not, or if a given pair of numbers is co-prime or not."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
